# Pi Package Conventions

## Package rules

- Use `packages/pi-{plugin-name}/` and colocate its metadata, docs, tests, and resources.
- Create only the resource directories the package provides, and keep the
  `files` and `pi` manifest entries aligned with them.

## Canonical layout

```text
packages/pi-{plugin-name}/
├── package.json
├── README.md
├── CHANGELOG.md
├── LICENSE
├── extensions/             # When the package provides an extension
│   └── {plugin-name}/
│       ├── index.ts
│       └── <implementation-file>.ts
├── skills/                 # When the package provides skills
│   └── <skill-name>/
│       └── SKILL.md
├── prompts/                # When the package provides prompts
│   └── <prompt-name>.md
├── themes/                 # When the package provides themes
│   └── <theme-name>.json
└── test/
```

## Manifest contract

Start from this shape; omit paths and `pi` keys for resource types the package does not provide:

```json
{
  "files": ["extensions/", "skills/", "prompts/", "themes/", "README.md", "CHANGELOG.md", "LICENSE"],
  "pi": {
    "extensions": ["./extensions/{plugin-name}/index.ts"],
    "skills": ["./skills"],
    "prompts": ["./prompts/*.md"],
    "themes": ["./themes/*.json"]
  }
}
```
